<title>USA: Computer Learning gets U.S. OK on school.</title>
<headline>Computer Learning gets U.S. OK on school.</headline>
<dateline>FAIRFAX, Va. 1997-01-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Computer Learning Centers Inc said the federal Department of Education had granted Title IV eligibility to the company's Laurel, Md., Learning Center.</p>
<p>The company said in a Friday statement the eligibility took effect Jan 22. Under Title IV qualified students attending the Laurel school are eligible to take part in various federally funded financial aid programs.</p>
<p>Computer Learning Centers provides computer-related education and training at 13 sites nationwide.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk, (212) 859-1610))</p>
